# Everything here is deployed to and executed on a Linux box. CRLF baked into
# a committed .sh (or the .service unit) breaks direct execution on that box
# (`#!/bin/bash\r: bad interpreter`) even though it looks fine in a Windows
# editor. Force LF for the whole tree so this can't recur regardless of local
# core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
